# ISO 21423 connector configuration (alternative to the InOrbit ROS2 agent, see README).
# Read by docker compose (env_file); keep the KEY=value format, no shell syntax.
# The robot's ISO entity UUID. It is also its OpenRobOps robot id, and must match
# metadata.id in oro-config/iso-robot.yaml (lowercase).
ISO_ENTITY_UUID=7b1a9c3e-1111-4222-8333-444455556666
# The facility coordinate system id. Must match `iso21423.ccs.id` in the OpenRobOps settings.
ISO_CCS_ID=0b1c2d3e-4f50-4a6b-8c7d-9e0f1a2b3c4d
# One of the OpenRobOps `robotApiKeys` (same value as INORBIT_KEY for the ROS2 agent).
# The connector reads it from the ORO_API_KEY environment variable (no key file needed).
ORO_API_KEY={APP_KEY}
ORO_URL=http://localdev.com:3000/
